# Accepted / non-exploitable vulnerabilities (reviewed).
# Each entry MUST carry a justification and a review date.

# CVE-2026-85393 — node-forge: RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature forgery on verification.
# No upstream fix exists (node-forge 1.4.0 is the latest release).
# Not exploitable here: node-forge is used ONLY to GENERATE the internal PKI
# (X.509 assembly, CRL signing, PKCS#12 bundling) and to parse our own PEMs in
# server/src/pki.js. The app never uses node-forge to VERIFY an externally
# supplied RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature — mTLS client-cert verification is performed
# by Traefik (Go), not by this process. Re-evaluate when node-forge ships a fix.
# Reviewed: 2026-10-08
CVE-2026-85393

# CVE-2026-111181 — body-parser 1.20.8 (HIGH), decompression stream DoS. Fix
# (1.20.9 / 2.4.0) is not yet available in the MS npm feed proxy (latest 1.20.8 / 2.3.0).
# Mitigated in server/src/index.js: requests with a non-identity Content-Encoding
# are rejected with 415 before the parser runs, so no decompression stream is created.
# TODO: bump express/body-parser once the feed carries 1.20.9+.
# Reviewed: 2026-10-24 (re-check by 2026-11-07)
CVE-2026-111181

# nodemailer 10.1.2 (MEDIUM) — addressparser quirks; fix 10.1.4 not yet in the MS feed.
# Not exploitable here: mail is only sent by monitoring.js to the admin-configured
# recipient (cfg.to); no attacker-controlled address strings are ever parsed.
# TODO: bump to >=10.1.4 once available. Reviewed: 2026-10-24 (re-check by 2026-11-07)
